WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.734
-The Republican Party
has gone all in

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:06.067
on the truly pathetic claim that
Silicon Valley Bank collapsed

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:09.133
not because of financial
deregulation they supported,

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:10.734
but because the bank was woke.

00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:13.234
In fact, they're desperately
trying to prop up

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:14.567
Florida governor Ron DeSantis,

00:00:14.567 --> 00:00:17.367
the GOP's leading opponent
of so-called wokeness,

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:20.200
with glowing profiles
and easy interviews on Fox News.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.334
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:24.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:27.634
Almost on a daily basis,

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:29.200
the conservative movement
finds itself

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.868
grasping for some dumb
new culture-war issue

00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:33.467
to get audiences outraged about.

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:35.567
They whined about gender-neutral
Potato Head dolls,

00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:37.534
woke LEGO sets,
and electric stoves,

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:40.601
and now they've moved on
to another mindless obsession --

00:00:40.601 --> 00:00:41.834
washing machines.

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:43.534
-First it was your gas stoves.

00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:47.000
Now the Biden administration
targeting your washer,

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.067
pushing new efficiency standards

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:51.934
as part of its global
climate agenda.

00:00:51.934 --> 00:00:55.100
-President Biden's policies
may aim to clean the planet,

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.467
but they'll leave your clothes
dirty and smelly.

00:00:57.467 --> 00:01:00.367
-I think we should attack them
on gas stoves.

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:03.200
That's the opening,
the kitchen wars.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.434
Why are dishwashers bad?
Why are washing machines bad?

00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:08.300
-What did I read today?
They're going after showers?

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.400
Wait, they're going after
some other goofy thing.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.667
-Yeah, washing machines.
-Laundry. Laundry.

00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:14.834
-Before long, you'll have to say
your preferred pronouns

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:16.200
to get your dishwasher to work.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:19.100
-First they want my stove.
Now they want my dishwasher.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.300
What's next? They gonna
take away my iron next?

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:24.234
I don't know.

00:01:24.234 --> 00:01:27.267
-Yeah, well, look, I'm someone
who does lots of laundry.

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:29.868
I do laundry
for six people every week.

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:31.501
And so I know
a little bit about this,

00:01:31.501 --> 00:01:34.167
and the last thing I need
is my laundry taking longer.

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:36.701
I'm already dealing
with a low-flow showerhead,

00:01:36.701 --> 00:01:38.400
and my kids are coming out
with conditioner

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.167
smashed to their head
like an old "Seinfeld" episode.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.667
And I have to tell them
to get back in and rewash.

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:46.934
I can't even flush my toilet one
time to get toilet paper down

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:48.801
because of the low-flow toilets.

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:50.767
-Old "Seinfeld" episode?
You think that's bad.

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:52.868
The other day, one of my kids
came running out of the bathroom

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:56.868
with his pants around his ankles
screaming, "Vandelay, Vandelay!"

00:01:56.868 --> 00:02:00.801
Thanks to Joe Biden, he lost
his job as a latex salesman.

00:02:00.801 --> 00:02:02.501
Also, are you listening
to yourself?

00:02:02.501 --> 00:02:05.000
If that was the plot
of an old "Seinfeld" episode,

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.701
then it can't be a new problem.

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:08.567
Thanks to Joe Biden's
woke policies,

00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:10.100
Americans are waiting for tables

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:12.634
at Chinese restaurants
for hours.

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:14.434
With that said,
I'm all for the Seinfeld'ing

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:15.601
of our political discourse.

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:17.968
I can't wait for Biden
to square off with Trump

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:19.067
at the presidential debates.

00:02:19.067 --> 00:02:20.067
[ As Biden ]
Now, listen up, Donald.

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:21.634
I got a phone call
the other day.

00:02:21.634 --> 00:02:25.400
And it was the jerk store.
No joke. I'm not kidding around.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:28.801
And they said to me, they said,
"It's the jerk store calling.

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:31.300
We're running out of you."
Come on, Jack.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.167
[ "Seinfeld" theme plays ]

00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:35.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.734
[ Normal voice ]
It's so funny to think
that Biden's the Seinfeld now

00:02:37.734 --> 00:02:42.167
when during the Obama era,
he was definitely the Kramer.

00:02:42.167 --> 00:02:43.734
What's that? You want to know
who everyone is now?

00:02:43.734 --> 00:02:45.834
Okay, Biden's the Seinfeld.
Kamala's the Elaine.

00:02:45.834 --> 00:02:48.000
Bernie's the George.
And Hunter is the Kramer.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.000
"Jerry, I can't find my laptop!"

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.834 --> 00:02:54.634
Also, one more tangent here.

00:02:54.634 --> 00:02:57.701
The only reasonable complaint
about modern appliances is this.

00:02:57.701 --> 00:02:59.934
Dishwashers are too quiet now.

00:02:59.934 --> 00:03:02.634
It used to be you knew when
your dishwasher was running,

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:04.434
so you never opened it
mid-cycle,

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:06.033
got sprayed with hot water

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:07.767
while your wife yelled
from upstairs,

00:03:07.767 --> 00:03:09.968
"Did you open
a running dishwasher again?"

00:03:09.968 --> 00:03:13.934
forcing you to yell back,
"I didn't hear anything!"

00:03:13.934 --> 00:03:16.734
Anyway, the GOP has
no discernible policy agenda

00:03:16.734 --> 00:03:18.267
aside from whining
about wokeness,

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:19.434
a term they can't even define.

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:20.901
As far as I can tell,

00:03:20.901 --> 00:03:23.167
wokeness to them just means
stuff they don't like.

00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:26.067
In fact, rather than define
the term "wokeness" for voters,

00:03:26.067 --> 00:03:28.601
they've already moved on
to coming up with newer

00:03:28.601 --> 00:03:30.901
and even dumber words to
describe things they don't like.

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:33.267
Ron DeSantis was campaigning
in Iowa over the weekend.

00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:36.234
He tried out this incredibly
stupid turn of phrase.

00:03:36.234 --> 00:03:40.434
-Because woke ideology has
infected so many institutions,

00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:42.901
if you really want to protect
the freedom of your folks,

00:03:42.901 --> 00:03:46.033
you got to be willing
to defend them against the left

00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:49.300
imposing their pathologies
on your people

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:50.968
in any of these institutions.

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:53.801
So we've got to fight
if we see it in medicine

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:56.334
or the universities
or the corporations.

00:03:56.334 --> 00:03:58.701
You can't just say, "Let it go,"

00:03:58.701 --> 00:04:01.033
because then
we're gonna be living

00:04:01.033 --> 00:04:03.200
under an oppressive
"woke-ocracy."

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.634
-Ooh.

00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:08.901
Well, that just rolls right off
the tongue -- woke-ocracy.

00:04:08.901 --> 00:04:11.200
Pretty sure saying that
gives you strep throat.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.601
The only -- only way
this makes sense

00:04:13.601 --> 00:04:16.267
is if it's a ploy by DeSantis
to come up with a new word

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:18.734
that's such a mouthful,
Donald Trump can't pronounce it

00:04:18.734 --> 00:04:20.834
and then melts down in a debate.

00:04:20.834 --> 00:04:22.567
[ As Trump ] You know, Ron,
he likes to talk about

00:04:22.567 --> 00:04:23.467
the woke-a-croky.

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:26.000
I mean the waka-crazy.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.033
I mean the waka-coca-racy-shock.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:29.601
Look, folks,
we're living in Wakanda.

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:31.934
We have to admit it.

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:33.968
We're living in Wakanda,
and if we're not careful,

00:04:33.968 --> 00:04:35.734
it's gonna be Wakanda forever.

00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:37.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.701 --> 00:04:39.634
[ Normal voice ] DeSantis's
obsession with battling wokeness

00:04:39.634 --> 00:04:41.667
has made him a subject
of fawning profiles

00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:43.934
and softball interviews
on Fox News.

00:04:43.934 --> 00:04:47.100
On Monday, he did an interview
with Fox host Brian Kilmeade

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:49.133
where they had a catch
at a baseball field.

00:04:49.133 --> 00:04:51.601
-We're on a baseball field.
You've had a busy day.

00:04:51.601 --> 00:04:52.901
But you wanted
to come to this field

00:04:52.901 --> 00:04:55.734
because it means so much to you,
obviously.

00:04:55.734 --> 00:04:57.968
Even though I'm a soccer player,
do you have time for a catch?

00:04:57.968 --> 00:05:00.100
-Let's do it. I'll do it.
Yeah, alright.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:02.734
-If not this time
to run for president,

00:05:02.734 --> 00:05:05.300
would you think at some time
it's safe to say

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:06.701
that that would be
one of your goals?

00:05:06.701 --> 00:05:10.601
-I would only --
I would only do stuff

00:05:10.601 --> 00:05:12.901
if I thought
there was a rationale for me

00:05:12.901 --> 00:05:15.400
to accomplish things
on behalf of the people.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.167
So it's all substance-driven
about whether I could serve

00:05:18.167 --> 00:05:20.367
or not serve
in a variety of capacities.

00:05:20.367 --> 00:05:24.000
-Oh, someone get a radar gun
on those guys.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.701
Somehow during the course
of that interview,

00:05:25.701 --> 00:05:28.467
three runners scored.

00:05:28.467 --> 00:05:30.868
This interview's the worst thing
to happen on a baseball field

00:05:30.868 --> 00:05:33.167
since Randy Johnson
exploded that bird.

00:05:33.167 --> 00:05:35.200
[ Audience groans ]

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.367 --> 00:05:41.534
If it had been DeSantis throwing
instead of Randy,

00:05:41.534 --> 00:05:44.067
that bird would have been fine.

00:05:44.067 --> 00:05:45.601
Light bruising at best.

00:05:45.601 --> 00:05:47.801
And look, I know that clip
is kind of a bummer.

00:05:47.801 --> 00:05:50.100
So if it helps,
that bird would have died

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:51.834
of old age by now anyway.

00:05:51.834 --> 00:05:54.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.334 --> 00:05:56.300
I said if it helped.

00:05:58.501 --> 00:06:01.734
But, yes, it's great to see Opie
and Sheriff Taylor over here

00:06:01.734 --> 00:06:04.400
enjoying the old
American tradition

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:06.601
that fathers and sons
have engaged in for decades --

00:06:06.601 --> 00:06:08.367
putting on your suits
and lapel mics

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:11.000
for a game of catch
in front of a camera crew.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:13.701
Also, of course, Fox picked
their saddest button-eyed bozo,

00:06:13.701 --> 00:06:15.667
Brian Kilmeade, to have a catch
with a politician.

00:06:15.667 --> 00:06:17.133
Kilmeade's probably
been dreaming about this.

00:06:17.133 --> 00:06:18.667
I would have loved
to have seen the pre-interview.

00:06:18.667 --> 00:06:20.567
"Alright, we're just gonna
toss the ball back and forth.

00:06:20.567 --> 00:06:22.434
I'll ask you about wokeness.
And one more thing.

00:06:22.434 --> 00:06:24.701
Is it okay if I call you Dad?"

00:06:24.701 --> 00:06:25.767
[ Laughter ]

00:06:25.767 --> 00:06:27.234
But that's how desperate

00:06:27.234 --> 00:06:29.934
the leaders of the conservative
movement are to embrace DeSantis

00:06:29.934 --> 00:06:32.033
and his crusade
against so-called wokeness.

00:06:32.033 --> 00:06:34.601
They are a thoroughly
unserious political movement.

00:06:34.601 --> 00:06:36.801
So whining about wokeness
is their answer for everything.

00:06:36.801 --> 00:06:38.300
For example, after the collapse

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:39.634
of Silicon Valley Bank
last week,

00:06:39.634 --> 00:06:42.334
Republicans didn't blame
financial deregulation

00:06:42.334 --> 00:06:44.701
or the recklessness
of venture-capitalist tech bros.

00:06:44.701 --> 00:06:45.601
They blamed wokeness.

00:06:45.601 --> 00:06:47.133
Senator Roger Marshall

00:06:47.133 --> 00:06:49.734
called SVB
"a woke California bank."

00:06:49.734 --> 00:06:51.067
Donald Trump Jr. tweeted...

00:06:54.567 --> 00:06:56.367
And Senator Josh Hawley
tweeted...

00:06:58.868 --> 00:07:02.334
Yeah, man, I'm tired of all
these radical leftist banks

00:07:02.334 --> 00:07:04.133
taking my money,

00:07:04.133 --> 00:07:07.300
spending it on woke products
like credit default swaps

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:08.634
and mortgage-backed securities.

00:07:08.634 --> 00:07:09.968
The other day -- true story --

00:07:09.968 --> 00:07:11.634
I asked to meet
with my banker at Chase,

00:07:11.634 --> 00:07:14.167
and when I walked in, who was
sitting across the desk from me?

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:16.367
None other than
the new green M&amp;M.

00:07:16.367 --> 00:07:19.634
And she told me the bank
invested all my money

00:07:19.634 --> 00:07:21.934
in a mutual fund that consists
of critical race theory

00:07:21.934 --> 00:07:23.100
and electric stoves.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:25.801
And then I knew my money
was really in trouble

00:07:25.801 --> 00:07:27.200
when I saw her get up
to grab a pen

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:28.667
and she wasn't wearing
high heels anymore.

00:07:28.667 --> 00:07:31.334
She was wearing...flats.

00:07:31.334 --> 00:07:33.133
[ Thunder crashes ]

00:07:33.133 --> 00:07:34.434
[ Evil screaming ]

00:07:34.434 --> 00:07:36.667
-[ Echoing ] Woke-ocracy.

00:07:36.667 --> 00:07:39.667
[ Laughter ]

00:07:39.667 --> 00:07:41.267
-This has to be one of
the silliest talking points

00:07:41.267 --> 00:07:42.834
I've ever heard in my life.

00:07:42.834 --> 00:07:44.734
The word "woke bank"
would honestly be so funny

00:07:44.734 --> 00:07:46.701
if they weren't
so deadly serious about it.

00:07:46.701 --> 00:07:47.968
If a bank can be woke,

00:07:47.968 --> 00:07:49.934
then that means
literally anything can be woke.

00:07:49.934 --> 00:07:51.467
And GOP senators
weren't the only ones

00:07:51.467 --> 00:07:52.667
pushing this pathetic narrative

00:07:52.667 --> 00:07:54.300
that wokeness
is somehow responsible

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:56.667
for a bank run caused entirely
by deregulation

00:07:56.667 --> 00:07:58.300
and reckless
venture-capitalist tech bros.

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:01.167
There was also Fox News,
which went so far as to blame

00:08:01.167 --> 00:08:04.501
the Obama administration
for the collapse of SVB.

00:08:04.501 --> 00:08:07.000
-Remember that after 2008,
the Obama administration,

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.267
Eric Holder, swooped in
and imposed DEI --

00:08:09.267 --> 00:08:11.434
diversity, equity,
and inclusion -- standards

00:08:11.434 --> 00:08:14.367
on the entire financial sector.

00:08:14.367 --> 00:08:16.467
And that's one of the main
reasons our big banks

00:08:16.467 --> 00:08:18.667
are now increasingly incompetent
and also one of the reasons

00:08:18.667 --> 00:08:21.534
Americans are so divided
by race.

00:08:21.534 --> 00:08:24.801
Ideologues used
the 2008 bank bailout

00:08:24.801 --> 00:08:27.067
to kill American meritocracy.

00:08:27.067 --> 00:08:29.300
-That's right,
they killed meritocracy

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:32.567
so they could replace it
with woke-acaca-roka-cracy.

00:08:32.567 --> 00:08:34.334
[ Laughter ]

00:08:34.334 --> 00:08:36.267
First of all,
the 2008 bailout was Bush.

00:08:36.267 --> 00:08:38.033
Second, do you know
how much harder

00:08:38.033 --> 00:08:39.300
Obama could have been
on the banks?

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:40.534
He could have nationalized them

00:08:40.534 --> 00:08:42.167
or restored
the Glass-Steagall division

00:08:42.167 --> 00:08:43.601
between commercial
and investment banking.

00:08:43.601 --> 00:08:46.467
But he didn't. You think
he secretly made them woke

00:08:46.467 --> 00:08:48.701
and that's why
they're collapsing now.

00:08:48.701 --> 00:08:50.467
[ As Obama ] Alright,
Goldman Sachs, listen up.

00:08:50.467 --> 00:08:52.801
You can have a bailout
and keep all the money.

00:08:52.801 --> 00:08:57.501
But in return, I'm gonna
make washing machines suck.

00:08:57.501 --> 00:08:59.100
And you're not going to
try to stop me.

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:00.667
[ Normal voice ] Now,
as we explained on Monday,

00:09:00.667 --> 00:09:02.467
the SVB collapse
was actually the fault

00:09:02.467 --> 00:09:05.133
of panicky tech VCs who rushed
to pull all their money out

00:09:05.133 --> 00:09:06.434
and a bipartisan push

00:09:06.434 --> 00:09:09.634
to repeal financial rules
for mid-sized banks back in 2018

00:09:09.634 --> 00:09:11.801
that was signed into law
by President Trump.

00:09:11.801 --> 00:09:14.067
In fact, you know who also voted

00:09:14.067 --> 00:09:15.901
to repeal those
Dodd-Frank reforms

00:09:15.901 --> 00:09:18.067
when he was a little-known
congressman from Florida?

00:09:18.067 --> 00:09:20.634
None other than
Ron "The Heater" DeSantis.

00:09:20.634 --> 00:09:23.234
That's right,
DeSantis voted with Trump

00:09:23.234 --> 00:09:25.801
to gut Wall Street
regulations in 2018.

00:09:25.801 --> 00:09:27.400
So it shouldn't be
surprising at all

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:29.601
that DeSantis is now
going on Fox News

00:09:29.601 --> 00:09:31.133
blaming the collapse on,
you guessed it,

00:09:31.133 --> 00:09:33.067
diversity, equity,
and inclusion.

00:09:33.067 --> 00:09:37.868
-I mean, this bank, they're so
concerned with DEI and politics

00:09:37.868 --> 00:09:39.434
and all kinds of stuff.

00:09:39.434 --> 00:09:41.300
I think that really diverted

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:43.767
from them focusing
on their core mission.

00:09:43.767 --> 00:09:45.434
-In fact, this bank was so woke,

00:09:45.434 --> 00:09:47.100
the CEO went on TV
the other day,

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:50.300
and he had shampoo
all over his head.

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:51.667
I mean, honestly, is anyone
buying this [bleep]

00:09:51.667 --> 00:09:52.767
What's next?
Oh, my God.

00:09:52.767 --> 00:09:54.133
Are they going to start
closing banks

00:09:54.133 --> 00:09:56.000
for woke new holidays
like Festivus?

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:58.567
Again, I didn't bring it up.

00:09:58.567 --> 00:10:00.601
As we noted on Monday,
it wasn't just Republicans

00:10:00.601 --> 00:10:02.234
who supported
the push to deregulate.

00:10:02.234 --> 00:10:03.601
Many centrist Democrats

00:10:03.601 --> 00:10:05.767
voted to repeal
the Dodd-Frank rules, too.

00:10:05.767 --> 00:10:08.868
Even Barney Frank, whose name
was on the original bill,

00:10:08.868 --> 00:10:11.567
ended up sitting on the board
of Signature Bank,

00:10:11.567 --> 00:10:14.000
which also collapsed,
and supported the push

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.667
to ease some of the financial
regulations he passed.

00:10:16.667 --> 00:10:18.033
Do you know how crazy that is?

00:10:18.033 --> 00:10:20.467
That's like if your name
was Mike Whirlpool

00:10:20.467 --> 00:10:22.834
and you wanted to abolish...
-Washing machines.

00:10:22.834 --> 00:10:25.100
-The few progressives
who loudly opposed the changes

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:27.234
included senators Bernie Sanders
and Elizabeth Warren.

00:10:27.234 --> 00:10:28.567
In fact, today,
Warren went on TV

00:10:28.567 --> 00:10:31.501
to talk about the 2018 law
repealing the requirements

00:10:31.501 --> 00:10:33.334
for mid-sized banks
to conduct stress tests,

00:10:33.334 --> 00:10:35.033
basically tests to make sure

00:10:35.033 --> 00:10:37.200
that banks have enough liquidity
or cash

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:38.467
to weather a storm
like this one.

00:10:38.467 --> 00:10:40.634
And when the anchor
suggested that banks

00:10:40.634 --> 00:10:42.767
were doing stress tests
on their own

00:10:42.767 --> 00:10:44.934
and didn't need government
regulators to oversee the tests,

00:10:44.934 --> 00:10:45.968
Warren laughed.

00:10:45.968 --> 00:10:47.400
-We've had a number
of those CEOs

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:52.100
on the shows in the last few
days -- Fifth Third, Schwab.

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:53.767
They do their own
stress testing.

00:10:53.767 --> 00:10:56.701
Not everyone was behaving
in a risk profile

00:10:56.701 --> 00:10:59.267
and a risk manner that
Silicon Valley Bank was.

00:10:59.267 --> 00:11:01.434
-[ Laughs ] I'm sorry.

00:11:01.434 --> 00:11:03.968
I taught school
for many, many years,

00:11:03.968 --> 00:11:06.701
and I did not let my students
do their own testing.

00:11:06.701 --> 00:11:08.734
-Of course not.

00:11:08.734 --> 00:11:10.868
You can't even let students
bring their tests home,

00:11:10.868 --> 00:11:12.467
or they'll turn an "F"
into an "A"

00:11:12.467 --> 00:11:14.534
before they show their parents.

00:11:14.534 --> 00:11:16.534
I'm willing to bet Warren
was one of those cool teachers

00:11:16.534 --> 00:11:17.634
who would grill her students

00:11:17.634 --> 00:11:19.200
but then give them
invaluable life guidance

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:20.701
while sitting backwards
on a chair.

00:11:20.701 --> 00:11:23.834
"You got talent, Brad,
but you got to use it.

00:11:23.834 --> 00:11:25.534
Now, what do you say
we go out back

00:11:25.534 --> 00:11:26.901
and take a hit off this joint?

00:11:26.901 --> 00:11:29.167
I know a good spot
by the baseball field.

00:11:29.167 --> 00:11:32.167
Only losers hang out there."

00:11:32.167 --> 00:11:33.934
The Republican Party
has once again revealed itself

00:11:33.934 --> 00:11:35.634
as a thoroughly
unserious political movement

00:11:35.634 --> 00:11:38.167
by blaming a banking crisis
they caused on wokeness,

00:11:38.167 --> 00:11:39.467
a term they can't even define.

00:11:39.467 --> 00:11:41.133
To put it politely,
Republicans are full

00:11:41.133 --> 00:11:43.367
of a certain substance
you might find sitting in...

00:11:43.367 --> 00:11:44.667
-Low-flow toilets.

00:11:44.667 --> 00:11:47.133
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:47.133 --> 00:11:49.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

